<title>GERMANY: RWE Energie 1995/96 pre-tax profit higher.</title>
<headline>RWE Energie 1995/96 pre-tax profit higher.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to end June 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit				   485 vs     433</p>
<p>Electricity produced</p>
<p>    (billions of kilowatts)		  124,300 vs 125,600</p>
<p>    Sales					   16,407 vs  16,710</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>    Electricity				   15,947 vs  16,334</p>
<p>    Gas						  296 vs     262</p>
<p>    Water						 57 vs	55</p>
<p>    District heating				 107 vs	59</p>
<p>    Payment to parent RWE AG	  370 vs     333</p>
<p>    Transfers to reserves			  115 vs     100</p>
<p>    Cash Flow					3,428 vs   3,101</p>
<p>    Investments				    2,186 vs   1,945</p>
<p>    No of employees			     21,769 vs  22,461</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German energy group is RWE Energie AG, the largest subsidiary of RWE AG. Pre-tax profit does not include profit transfer. Profit transfer includes a dividend of 20 percent on existing capital.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
